    "name": "luh-trajectories-in-a-shared-space",
    "notes": "## The data contains trajectories and basic information about road users in a shared space.\r\n \r\n### Trajectories are denoted with time step, object id, x-coordinate, y-coordinate, and user type. Each time step last 0.5 seconds. Coordinates are in pixel and can be transferred to real-world scale using the scale provided. There are three types of users: pedestrian, cyclist, and vehicle.\r\n\r\n### In addition, the data also provides demographic attributes for road users. Pedestrians walking in groups are annotated.",
